- The user said “really nothing out of all the tasks got done” and accepted only contrast as meaningful coding work -> distinguish sharply between code changes, tests/probes, runtime housekeeping, milestone progress, and completed tracker tasks.
- The user expected parallelization across different app features, not merely parallel agents on a shared prerequisite gate -> parallelize independently closable product tasks once dependencies are clear, and close/commit one task before expanding scope.

Key steps:
