  1689	
  1690	### 16.0 Dispatch contract and cost-aware model manifest
  1691	
  1692	Every implementation dispatch copies this complete contract into the agent prompt. A heading in
  1693	this document is not sufficient authorization.
  1694	
  1695	1. Record base SHA, assigned owned paths, forbidden controller seams, dependencies, exact existing
  1696	   symbols, exact new symbols, ordered edits, focused tests, native acceptance, stop conditions,
  1697	   and the return-receipt template.
  1698	2. Use `fork_turns: "none"` and the explicit model/reasoning pair below. Never silently substitute
  1699	   Terra, an unrequested reasoning level, or an unspecified model. Luna Fast is preferred, never
  1700	   blocking: request `service_tier: "fast"` when the native spawn API exposes it; otherwise
  1701	   continue with explicit Luna Max/max/no-fork and do not claim Fast.
  1702	3. Feature agents edit only their leased files. They return exact integration receipts for
  1703	   `main.rs`, `tauriSource.ts`, public conversation/session/orchestration types, Settings, shell
  1704	   rosters, Tauri capabilities, package/Cargo manifests, and lockfiles. The controller applies
  1705	   each shared seam once after review.
  1706	4. No agent creates a second runtime, conversation store, orchestration ledger/reducer, Paneview
  1707	   factory/layout store, Dockview roster, settings authority, worktree authority, terminal
  1708	   registry, Browser child-view owner, resource owner, usage index, or confirmation executor.
  1709	5. No more than two build/test-heavy agents run concurrently; the default is one. Provider-native,
  1710	   Browser-native, and final Tauri proofs are serialized. A feature-agent packet may author focused
  1711	   tests but runs heavy commands only when the controller explicitly assigns a runner slot.
  1712	6. Every data lane repeats the hard query rule: filtering, joins, grouping, aggregation, sorting,
  1713	   and paging execute DB-side in one translated SQL query or database view; no materialize-then-
  1714	   shape, client evaluation, lazy loading, per-row follow-up, or N+1. Inspect generated SQL, add a
  1715	   view plus covering index when translation is insufficient, sweep sibling paths, and keep a
  1716	   roughly 20-row page to 1-3 total DB queries.
  1717	7. Whoever opens a Browser/native proof session stops that exact named daemon/process tree before
  1718	   returning. Whoever creates a worktree removes and prunes it immediately after merge,
  1719	   cherry-pick, push-to-PR, or abandonment; dirty/locked/unmerged trees are reported with exact
  1720	   path, branch, status, reason, and owner rather than deleted.
