     5	 * A language server is the background program that knows what the code MEANS:
     6	 * where a name is defined, what is wrong with a file, what the inline type
     7	 * hints are. For a large C# solution it can spend the first half-minute after
     8	 * start-up just reading the project, and everything asked of it in that window
     9	 * either comes back empty or arrives very late. Until now the editor said
    10	 * nothing about that, so a slow start looked like a broken feature.
